IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part1-application`
IMPORT `au-part4-repeal`
IMPORT `au-part5-interpretation`
IMPORT `au-part6-service`
IMPORT `au-part7-powers`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia), compilation C2026C00117 (28 March 2026) --
-- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under an Act (to apply, object, appeal, reply
-- or pay), or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period
-- ends and which of their days count. One person, one Act, one time limit at a time.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions
-- that person asks. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every answer is one call
-- of a module rule. What this layer does is (a) turn the person's plain answers into the
-- records and lists the modules expect, and (b) in the few places where two module rules must
-- be put together to give one answer (a counted period, and then the rest-day rule on its last
-- day), call them in turn.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes one input per fact the person can state: a day, a number,
-- yes or no, a choice from a list, or a list of days. The two lists a person must supply for
-- any period are the PUBLIC HOLIDAYS in the place where the thing is to be done (the Act does
-- not list them, so no list in this encoding can be complete) and the days the office is
-- CLOSED for the whole day (s 36(3)). Section 36(3) treats both the same way, as a "holiday",
-- so the person gives ONE list of such days, and the module's rule is called with that list
-- as its public holidays and an empty list of closures. (A single list, placed last among a
-- question's inputs, is also all that `l4 batch` of 1.6.98 can re-print; see NOTES.md.)
-- A person who does not know of any gives an empty list.
--
-- THE OTHER PARTY. The person's period is almost always a duty or a liability towards an
-- official (the Minister, a tribunal, the authority that made the decision). The official is
-- never a seat. Where the text gives the person a privilege, a power or a claim against the
-- official, the inputs include the facts about the official on which it depends (whether the
-- appointer has directed otherwise, whether the Minister has granted an extension, on which
-- day the Minister received the report). See ## Jural relations in NOTES.md.
--
-- WHAT THE ACT DOES NOT SAY. It never says how long a "week" or a "year" is. The question
-- "On which day does my period end?" answers NOTHING for a period in weeks or years. The
-- separate question that reads a week as 7 days and a year as 12 months says in its title that
-- the Act does not state that reading.

-- Turns a day on which a sitting began into the record the modules expect. The person gives only
-- the day a sitting BEGAN; a sitting that runs past midnight is part of the day it began (s 2M(2)),
-- so its adjournment day is not asked and is set to the same day as a placeholder that the
-- sitting-day rules never read (they count only `begins on`).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A sitting of a House`
`a sitting of the House that began on` d MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF d, d

§ `Acts Interpretation Act 1901 -- the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `Whether this Act applies to the Act that binds me (s 2)`

-- s 2(1) and (2). This Act applies to every Act, itself included, unless the Act (or the
-- provision) in question shows a contrary intention. The person cannot tell whether an Act shows
-- one without reading it, so it is a fact the person states.
@export Does the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 apply to the Act that binds me (s 2)?
GIVEN `the Act shows an intention that the Acts Interpretation Act is not to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act that binds you, or the provision you are asking about, show an intention that the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 is not to apply to it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 apply to the Act that binds me` IS
    `a provision of this Act applies to the Act or provision` `the Act shows an intention that the Acts Interpretation Act is not to apply`

§§ `Business days, financial years and sitting days (ss 2B, 2M)`

-- s 2B "business day". A day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday. (This is not
-- the same as the "holiday" of s 36(3), which also counts days the office is closed.)
@export Is this day a business day (s 2B)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `public holidays where the thing is to be done` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do the thing? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a business day` IS
    `is a business day` `the day I am asking about` `public holidays where the thing is to be done`

-- s 2B "financial year": a period of 12 months starting on 1 July.
@export On which day does the financial year that includes my day end (s 2B)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the financial year that includes my day end` IS
    (`the financial year containing` `the day I am asking about`)'s `last day`

-- s 2M, with s 36(1) item 6. "N sitting days after" a day is the N-th sitting day that falls
-- strictly after it. A sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.
@export Which day is the Nth sitting day of the House after my day (ss 2M, 36)?
GIVEN `the number of sitting days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many sitting days after your day?
      `the day I am counting from` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you counting from?
      `days a sitting of the House began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did (or will) a sitting of the House begin? (List each day; a sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Which day is the Nth sitting day of the House after my day` IS
    `the sitting day that is the n-th after` `the number of sitting days` `the day I am counting from` sittings
    WHERE
        sittings MEANS map `a sitting of the House that began on` `days a sitting of the House began`

§§ `When the Act or instrument that binds me comes into operation (ss 3, 3A)`

-- Only for a person who needs to know when something takes effect. The answer is NOTHING
-- where the text does not give a day: an instrument other than an Act with no stated day, or an
-- Act whose day has not yet been fixed.
DECLARE `What the enactment says about its own commencement` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `a particular day`
    `a day to be fixed later, not yet fixed`
    `a day that has since been fixed`

@export On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation (ss 3, 3A)?
GIVEN `what kind of enactment it is` IS A `Kind of enactment` @desc Is it an Act, an Act to alter the Constitution, a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument, or another instrument made under a power?
      `what it says about when it commences` IS A `What the enactment says about its own commencement` @desc What does it say about when it commences: nothing, a particular day, a day to be fixed later (not yet fixed), or a day that has since been fixed?
      `the day it names or that has since been fixed` IS A DATE @desc If it names a day, or a day has since been fixed, which day is that? (Give any day if neither applies.)
      `the day it received Royal Assent or was made` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act receive the Royal Assent, or the instrument get made?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` IS
    `the day the enactment commences` `what kind of enactment it is` says `the day it received Royal Assent or was made`
    WHERE
        says MEANS
            CONSIDER `what it says about when it commences`
            WHEN `nothing` THEN `silent about commencement`
            WHEN `a particular day` THEN `commencement on a particular day` `the day it names or that has since been fixed`
            WHEN `a day to be fixed later, not yet fixed` THEN `commencement on a day still to be fixed`
            WHEN `a day that has since been fixed` THEN `commencement on a day fixed later` `the day it names or that has since been fixed`

@export At what moment does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation (ss 3, 3A)?
GIVEN `what kind of enactment it is` IS A `Kind of enactment` @desc Is it an Act, an Act to alter the Constitution, a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument, or another instrument made under a power?
      `what it says about when it commences` IS A `What the enactment says about its own commencement` @desc What does it say about when it commences: nothing, a particular day, a day to be fixed later (not yet fixed), or a day that has since been fixed?
      `the day it names or that has since been fixed` IS A DATE @desc If it names a day, or a day has since been fixed, which day is that? (Give any day if neither applies.)
      `the day it received Royal Assent or was made` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act receive the Royal Assent, or the instrument get made?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `At what moment does the Act or instrument that binds me come into operation` IS
    `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `what kind of enactment it is` says `the day it received Royal Assent or was made`
    WHERE
        says MEANS
            CONSIDER `what it says about when it commences`
            WHEN `nothing` THEN `silent about commencement`
            WHEN `a particular day` THEN `commencement on a particular day` `the day it names or that has since been fixed`
            WHEN `a day to be fixed later, not yet fixed` THEN `commencement on a day still to be fixed`
            WHEN `a day that has since been fixed` THEN `commencement on a day fixed later` `the day it names or that has since been fixed`

§§ `What happens to what I already have or owe if an Act is repealed or amended (s 7)`

-- Only for a person asking about an Act that has been repealed or amended.
@export What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `the thing I am asking about` IS A `Kind of thing the repeal or amendment may touch` @desc What are you asking about: something not in force at the time, how the Act operated before, a right or liability you had acquired or incurred, a penalty for an offence you committed, or a proceeding or remedy about one of those?
      `the repealing or amending Act shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the repealing or amending Act show an intention that this should not be so?
GIVETH A `What becomes of the thing`
DECIDE `What happens to what I already have or owe when the Act is repealed or amended` IS
    `what a repeal or amendment does to` `the thing I am asking about` `the repealing or amending Act shows a contrary intention`

@export Does repealing the Act that repealed my old Act bring my old Act back (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `the repealing Act makes express provision for the old Act to revive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act that repeals the repealing Act say, in express words, that the old Act is revived?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does repealing the Act that repealed my old Act bring my old Act back` IS
    `the repeal of the repealing Act or part revives the old Act or part` `the repealing Act makes express provision for the old Act to revive`

§§ `The form I must use and the reasons I must be given (ss 25C, 25D)`

-- s 25C. Where an Act prescribes a form, substantial compliance is enough.
@export Does my form meet the requirement if it does not comply strictly with the prescribed form (s 25C)?
GIVEN `an Act prescribes the form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act prescribe the form you must use?
      `my form substantially complies with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your form substantially comply with the prescribed form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my form meet the requirement if it does not comply strictly with the prescribed form` IS
    `the form requirement is met` `an Act prescribes the form` `my form substantially complies with it`

-- s 25D. The decision-maker's duty, and so the person's claim: written reasons that set out the
-- findings on material questions of fact and refer to the evidence on which they were based.
@export Are the written reasons I was given complete (s 25D)?
GIVEN `an Act requires the decision-maker to give written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require the person or body who decided to give written reasons?
      `the reasons set out the findings on material questions of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the reasons set out the findings on the material questions of fact?
      `the reasons refer to the evidence on which the findings were based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the reasons refer to the evidence or other material on which those findings were based?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the written reasons I was given complete` IS
    `the written reasons are complete` `an Act requires the decision-maker to give written reasons` `the reasons set out the findings on material questions of fact` `the reasons refer to the evidence on which the findings were based`

§§ `Documents served on me (ss 28A, 29)`

-- s 28A. The sender's power to serve, and the person's liability to be served, by the listed
-- methods, or by another method another law or a court has authorised.
@export Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows (s 28A)?
GIVEN `whether I am a natural person or a body corporate` IS A `Kind of person served` @desc Are you a natural person or a body corporate?
      `how the document was served` IS A `Method of service` @desc How was the document served: delivered to you personally, left at your address, posted to your address, left at the head office, posted to the head office, or in some other way?
      `another law or a court order allows that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law, or an order of a court, allow service in that way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the document served on me in a way the Acts Interpretation Act allows` IS
    `service by this method is permitted` `whether I am a natural person or a body corporate` `how the document was served` `another law or a court order allows that way`

-- s 29. The day service by post is taken to be effected: the day the letter would be delivered
-- in the ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved.
@export On which day am I taken to have been served by post (s 29)?
GIVEN `the document was properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document properly addressed to you?
      `the postage was prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the postage prepaid?
      `it was posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it posted as a letter?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On which day would a letter posted at that time normally be delivered?
      `I can prove it reached me on a different day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that it reached you on a different day?
      `the day it did reach me` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day did it reach you? (Give any day if you cannot prove a different day.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` IS
    `the day service by post is taken to be effected` `the document was properly addressed` `the postage was prepaid` `it was posted as a letter` `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` proved
    WHERE
        proved MEANS IF `I can prove it reached me on a different day` THEN JUST `the day it did reach me` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Acting in an office (ss 33(4), 33A)`

-- Only for a person appointed to act in an office. The appointer's power to appoint, direct and
-- terminate is the person's liability; the person's privilege to act ends on the days below.
@export Until which day may I keep acting in a vacant office (s 33A(1)(ba))?
GIVEN `the first day I acted` IS A DATE @desc On which day did you start acting in the vacant office?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which day may I keep acting in a vacant office` IS
    `the last day the appointee may act in a vacant office` `the first day I acted`

@export Until which day may I keep acting after the office I was acting in became vacant (s 33A(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the day the office became vacant` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the office you were acting in become vacant?
      `the appointer has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who appointed you directed otherwise?
      `the day the appointer directed otherwise` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day? (Give any day if not.)
      `the vacancy has been filled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the vacancy been filled?
      `the day the vacancy was filled` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day? (Give any day if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which day may I keep acting after the office I was acting in became vacant` IS
    `the day the continued acting ends` `the day the office became vacant` directed filled
    WHERE
        directed MEANS IF `the appointer has directed otherwise` THEN JUST `the day the appointer directed otherwise` ELSE NOTHING
        filled MEANS IF `the vacancy has been filled` THEN JUST `the day the vacancy was filled` ELSE NOTHING

@export On which day do the 12 months of an appointment to act under a power to appoint run out (s 33(4))?
GIVEN `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the office or place created, or did it become vacant?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day do the 12 months of an appointment to act under a power to appoint run out` IS
    `the last day of the 12 months for an acting appointment under section 33(4)` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant`

§§ `A periodic report to a Minister (s 34C)`

-- Only for a person (including a body) whom an Act requires to furnish a periodic report to a
-- Minister. The person's duty is the Minister's claim; the person's power to ask for more time is
-- the Minister's liability; the Minister's power to grant it is the person's liability.
-- The Australian Secret Intelligence Service is outside the section altogether (s 34C(8)).
@export By which day must I furnish my periodic report to the Minister (s 34C(2))?
GIVEN `the Act sets its own period for furnishing the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act that requires the report set a period within which it must be furnished?
      `the last day of the period the report covers` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the period that the report covers end?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I furnish my periodic report to the Minister` IS
    `the last day to furnish a periodic report to the Minister` `the Act sets its own period for furnishing the report` `the last day of the period the report covers` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export Can I still ask the Minister for more time to furnish my report (s 34C(4))?
GIVEN `I think it will not be reasonably possible to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to furnish the report in the specified period?
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc On which day are you applying (or did you apply)?
      `the first day of the specified period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the specified period begin?
      `the last day of the specified period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the specified period end?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still ask the Minister for more time to furnish my report` IS
    `the person may apply for an extension` `I think it will not be reasonably possible to comply` `the day I apply` `the first day of the specified period` `the last day of the specified period` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export By which day must I explain in writing why my report was late (s 34C(7))?
GIVEN `the last day of the specified period or extension` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the period for furnishing the report, or the extension of it, end?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I explain in writing why my report was late` IS
    `the last day to furnish the statement explaining why the report was late` `the last day of the specified period or extension` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

-- What the person is owed: the Minister's duty to lay the report before each House. The days
-- are those of the House concerned: ask once for each House.
@export By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House, when no extension was granted (s 34C(3))?
GIVEN `who is furnishing the report` IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report` @desc Who is furnishing the report: an ordinary reporting person, ASIO, the Australian Signals Directorate, the Office of National Intelligence, or the Australian Secret Intelligence Service?
      `the day the Minister received my report` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Minister receive your report?
      `days a sitting of the House began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did (or will) a sitting of that House begin? (List each day; a sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when no extension was granted` IS
    IF   `section 34C applies to` `who is furnishing the report` AND `subsection 34C(3) applies to` `who is furnishing the report`
    THEN `the last day for the Minister to lay the report before a House` `the day the Minister received my report` sittings
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        sittings MEANS map `a sitting of the House that began on` `days a sitting of the House began`

@export By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House, when an extension was granted (s 34C(6)(c))?
GIVEN `who is furnishing the report` IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report` @desc Who is furnishing the report: an ordinary reporting person, ASIO, the Australian Signals Directorate, the Office of National Intelligence, or the Australian Secret Intelligence Service?
      `the day the Minister received my report` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Minister receive your report?
      `days a sitting of the House began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did (or will) a sitting of that House begin? (List each day; a sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must the Minister lay my report before a House when an extension was granted` IS
    IF   `section 34C applies to` `who is furnishing the report`
    THEN `the last day for the Minister to lay the extended report before a House` `who is furnishing the report` `the day the Minister received my report` sittings
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        sittings MEANS map `a sitting of the House that began on` `days a sitting of the House began`

@export By which day must the Minister lay my explanation and the extension before a House (s 34C(6)(a))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister granted me the extension` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Minister grant you the extension?
      `days a sitting of the House began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did (or will) a sitting of that House begin? (List each day; a sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must the Minister lay my explanation and the extension before a House` IS
    `the last day for the Minister to lay the extension statement before a House` `the day the Minister granted me the extension` sittings
    WHERE
        sittings MEANS map `a sitting of the House that began on` `days a sitting of the House began`

@export By which day must the Minister lay my explanation for a late report before a House (s 34C(7)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister received my explanation` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Minister receive your written explanation?
      `days a sitting of the House began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days did (or will) a sitting of that House begin? (List each day; a sitting that runs past midnight counts only for the day it began.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must the Minister lay my explanation for a late report before a House` IS
    `the last day for the Minister to lay the late-report statement before a House` `the day the Minister received my explanation` sittings
    WHERE
        sittings MEANS map `a sitting of the House that began on` `days a sitting of the House began`

§§ `Counting my time (ss 36, 37A)`

-- THE CORE QUESTIONS. How the Act words the period decides whether the day it counts from is
-- part of the period (s 36(1) items 5 and 6: "from" and "after" a day leave that day out). The
-- last day of the period is then moved to the next day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a
-- holiday where the Act requires or allows the thing to be done (s 36(2)). "Holiday" is a public
-- holiday where the thing is to be done, or a day the office is closed for the whole day (s 36(3)).
@export Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `how my period is worded in the Act` IS A `How a period is expressed` @desc How does the Act word the period: between two days, begins at, on or with a day, continues until a day, ends at, on or with a day, begins from a day, begins after a day, or ends before a day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the day I am counting from count as part of my period` IS
    `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `how my period is worded in the Act`

@export On which day does my period begin (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `the day my period is counted from or to` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the Act name when it words the period?
      `how my period is worded in the Act` IS A `How a period is expressed` @desc How does the Act word the period: between two days, begins at, on or with a day, continues until a day, ends at, on or with a day, begins from a day, begins after a day, or ends before a day?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period begin` IS
    `the first day of the period` `how my period is worded in the Act` `the day my period is counted from or to`

@export On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end (ss 2G, 36)?
GIVEN `the day my period is counted from or to` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the Act name when it words the period?
      `how my period is worded in the Act` IS A `How a period is expressed` @desc How does the Act word the period: between two days, begins at, on or with a day, continues until a day, ends at, on or with a day, begins from a day, begins after a day, or ends before a day?
      `the number of units in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days, weeks, months or years is the period?
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require or allow you to do the thing (apply, object, appeal, reply or pay) within this period?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period of days, weeks, months or years end` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of a counted period of` `the number of units in my period` `the unit my period is counted in` `that` `how my period is worded in the Act` `the day my period is counted from or to`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the last day on which the thing may be done` `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` last closures)
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

-- NOT STATED BY THE ACT. The Act never says how long a week or a year is. If a week were counted
-- as 7 days and a year as 12 months, this is the day on which the period would end.
@export On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months (a reading the Act does not state)?
GIVEN `the day my period is counted from or to` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the Act name when it words the period?
      `how my period is worded in the Act` IS A `How a period is expressed` @desc How does the Act word the period: between two days, begins at, on or with a day, continues until a day, ends at, on or with a day, begins from a day, begins after a day, or ends before a day?
      `the number of units in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days, weeks, months or years is the period?
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require or allow you to do the thing (apply, object, appeal, reply or pay) within this period?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day would my period end if a week were 7 days and a year were 12 months` IS
    CONSIDER `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `how my period is worded in the Act` `the day my period is counted from or to` `the number of units in my period` `the unit my period is counted in`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the last day on which the thing may be done` `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` last closures)
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at, with, or before a named day (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `the day my period is counted from or to` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the Act name when it words the period?
      `how my period is worded in the Act` IS A `How a period is expressed` @desc How does the Act word the period: between two days, begins at, on or with a day, continues until a day, ends at, on or with a day, begins from a day, begins after a day, or ends before a day?
      `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require or allow you to do the thing (apply, object, appeal, reply or pay) within this period?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end when the Act ends it at with or before a named day` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period` `how my period is worded in the Act` `the day my period is counted from or to`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the last day on which the thing may be done` `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` last closures)
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on, because it is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday (s 36(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period end, counting only days?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the last day of my period a day I cannot act on because it is a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` IS
    `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` `the last day of my period` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export What is the last day on which I may act, if my period ends on a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday (s 36(2))?
GIVEN `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require or allow you to do the thing (apply, object, appeal, reply or pay) within this period?
      `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period end, counting only days?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day on which I may act if my period ends on a Saturday a Sunday or a holiday` IS
    `the last day on which the thing may be done` `the Act requires or allows me to do the thing` `the last day of my period` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

@export Am I in time if I act on this day (s 36)?
GIVEN `the day I act` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you act (or did you act)?
      `the first day of my period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period begin?
      `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period end, counting only days?
      `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days are public holidays in the place where you must do it, or days on which the office is closed for the whole day? (List them, or give none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time if I act on this day` IS
    `the thing is done within the time allowed` `the day I act` `the first day of my period` `the last day of my period` closures
    WHERE
        closures MEANS `Days of closure` OF `public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day`, (LIST)

-- s 37A. A person attains a given age at the START of the anniversary of the date of birth.
-- NOTHING for a birth on 29 February where the anniversary year has no 29 February: the Act
-- does not say.
@export At what moment do I attain a given age (s 37A)?
GIVEN `the day I was born` IS A DATE @desc On which day were you born?
      `the age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Which age, in whole years, are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `At what moment do I attain a given age` IS
    `the moment a person attains the age` `the day I was born` `the age in years`
